Message-ID: <27d1e6020807141452q3b80339ey9b56b628818ccae5@mail.gmail.com>

Someone else reported on this list a similar sounding problem not so long ago.


The problem might be caused by manipulating a stale pointer to an R object
(that is an object that was discarded during R's garbage collection),
and troubleshooting this will likely mean running things through a C debugger.
You could try starting up you embedded R process with '--verbose' and see
if the problem happens right after garbage collection.
Without having further details on the exact code ran, it is difficult
to say more.





